Use the facts presented to decide. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {4, 7, 9, 14, 19, 23, 25, 26, 28, 30};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 25) return steps; if (a[mid] < 25) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

Choose the best answer to this. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {5, 7, 0, 9, -1, 1, -2};
int acc = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i += 2) acc += a[i];
return acc;

During a bench check, a technician traces the evidence: The case below gives the figures. What does this string routine return?
String s = "buzoyyca";
int acc = 0, target = 'a';
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) if (s.charAt(i) == target) acc++;
return acc;

In a review packet, a technician traces the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Apply your knowledge to the following. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {0, 1, 5, 6, 8, 10, 11, 12};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 1) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 1) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

Think through this worked case. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(15);
Node b = new Node(25);
Node c = new Node(5);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

Using the given data, answer this. Tracing this code:
