int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 19) return steps; if (a[mid] < 19) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

On a work order, an analyst traces the evidence: The case below gives the figures. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {-3, -1, 5, -4, 7, -3, 9, 6, 8};
int acc = a[0];
for (int i = 1; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] > acc) acc = a[i];
return acc;

Given the details below, respond. What does this string routine return?
String s = "cdzzoy";
int acc = 0, target = 'c';
for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) if (s.charAt(i) == target) acc++;
return acc;

In a technical note, an analyst traces the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Which index pair does this scan return?
int[] a = {1, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 17, 20};
int i = 0, j = a.length - 1;
while (i < j) { int s = a[i] + a[j]; if (s == 10) return new int[]{i, j}; if (s < 10) i++; else j--; }
return new int[]{-1, -1};

In a reference guide, an analyst traces the evidence: The case below gives the figures. Work out the answer to this item. What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(20);
